# Friday decisions

Rishabh Sharma owns Friday. The spoken address is Sir.

## Now

- Build and run on this Mac. Ship the same program later to the spare Linux laptop.
- Spare laptop: Linux, 8 GB RAM, 500 GB SSD. It is the always-on brain.
- Model: Ollama `qwen2.5:3b` with a short context. A 7B model does not fit that laptop beside voice.
- Devices reach the brain later through Tailscale. They need internet. They do not need the same Wi-Fi.
- Voice libraries need Python 3.14. The Mac's default `python3` is 3.15, which cannot install them yet, so voice runs from `.venv`.
- Current slice: voice, plus a web lookup. If Friday does not know a fact, he asks before searching. A following yes or no does not need the name. The lookup is DuckDuckGo, because Google's own API needs a key. Spoken replies use OpenAI gpt-4o-mini-tts when OPENAI_API_KEY is set, and Piper when it is not. Calendar is not connected.

## Later, only when that step starts

- Google Calendar, after he can sign in with a personal Google account.
- A separate wake-word model, so he can hear the name without transcribing every sound.
- Phones are tap-to-talk over Tailscale.
- Outlook and Teams both need an app in the work tenant, signed in as Rishabh. He cannot register one. Both wait until an admin creates the app. Mail is the first permission to ask for. Teams chat permissions are stricter, not a way around the lock. Send only after he confirms.
- One device is "speak here" at a time.
- CI comes after the program runs on the spare laptop.

## Leave alone during the current slice

Do not add Docker, a web UI, Graph, or a pipeline in this slice.
